# Pairs with NoResurrection. Retiring the old copy lifts its fence instead of
# keeping every captured shard fenced, so a router that cached the old copy is
# served it again after a newer write landed on the resized copy.
MODULE: NoResurrectionRetireDropsFence
TARGET: NoResurrection
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: retiring the old copy lifts its fence, so a stale reader is served the old copy again
PERTURBS: ResizeRetire

--- FIND
    /\ rz = "swapped"
    /\ fence' = rzShards
--- REPLACE
    /\ rz = "swapped"
\* MUTATION: the soft-deleted copy is unfenced.
    /\ fence' = {}
--- END
